# ComposeIO Spec Checklist — standing rules for ComposeIO spec changes [SPEC:CXC-SPEC-CHECKLIST]

> A small checklist, one node per rule. Rule 1 is decided (Plumb's addendum, accepted by the architect). The other rules are the candidate rules the spec audit of the shared plug-in contract (spec 95) suggested, quoted as the audit wrote them, plus one from Plumb's review, each proposed until the architect ratifies it.

---

## 1. Placement

### [CXC-SCL-PLACEMENT] Placement is UNRATIFIED, and filename 96 was verified unused

- placement-status: UNRATIFIED. Written into `corpora/platform-specs/` beside spec 95, whose `CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION` says this checklist is created before the build; see [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT] for the directory's numbering convention.
- filename-number-check: `96` was verified unused across `corpora/platform-specs/` before this file was written (listing 2026-11-26: 95 taken by `95-plugin-contract.lts`, 97 and 98 free, 99 the reserved conventions-document number).
- dropped-rules: the audit's rules E15 (HA key lists) and E16 (install-time warnings) were dropped at the architect's ruling of 2026-11-26, because they describe the accept-and-ignore key list and install-record warnings that spec 95 r4 removed.
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SPEC-CHECKLIST]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT], [CXC-PC-PLACEMENT]

---

## 2. The decided rule

### [CXC-SCL-HOST-CITES-VERSION] Rule 1: a host-side change cites the contract version it implements

- rule: "a host-side change cites the contract version it implements."
- applies-to: every ComposeIO host-side change and, by the same standing order, Gnomon's GM-SPEC-CHECKLIST (which gains the same rule; that file is not edited here).
- verify-machine: each host-side change record (spec revision, commit message or decision node) names one `plugin-contract-vX.Y` tag, and a check over the change set finds no host-side change without it.
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — Plumb's addendum, accepted by the architect
- provenance: Plumb's addendum to the brief, accepted by the architect (2026-11-26); see [CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SPEC-CHECKLIST]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION], [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS]

---

## 3. Candidate rules from the audit of spec 95

